{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "SARH Orders Console API",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "description": "واجهة تجربة الباك محليًا / Local backend API playground.\n\n**Quick walkthrough:**\n1. Auth → login → Try it out → choose Admin or Agent → Execute.\n2. Products → GET: copy a product `_id` and `unitPriceMinor`.\n3. Order attempts → POST with `{}`: copy `_id` and `operationKey`.\n4. Orders → POST: use that `_id` as `attemptId`, put `operationKey` in `Idempotency-Key`, and fill the order with the product values.\n5. Execute the identical create request again: response is `200` with the SAME order ID, not a new order.\n6. Acknowledge successful creation using `previousAttemptId` when preparing the next form.\n\nSwagger UI adds `X-SARH-Request: 1` automatically. Open this UI on the same origin as the API (normally http://localhost:4000/docs/); the browser sends Origin and manages the HttpOnly cookie. Do not paste a cookie in Authorize: browsers cannot manually set that forbidden header. Standalone clients should use their own cookie jar and an Origin from APP_ORIGINS plus the custom header.\n\nAmounts are integer **halalas**, currency SAR. Dates are UTC. Admin routes are labeled. These calls affect the local development database."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "/",
      "description": "Same origin as Swagger UI (keeps login cookies working)"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Health"
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth"
    },
    {
      "name": "Products"
    },
    {
      "name": "Order attempts"
    },
    {
      "name": "Orders"
    },
    {
      "name": "Users"
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "cookieAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
